==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|socle}}, from {{der|en|it|zoccolo||wooden shoe}}, from {{der|en|la|socculus}}, diminutive of {{m|la|soccus||sock}}. {{doublet|en|zoccolo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsoʊkəl/}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊkəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{lb|en|architectural element}} A low [[plinth]] or [[pedestal]] used to display a statue or other artwork.
# {{lb|en|architectural element}} A plain face or plinth at the foot of a wall.
# {{lb|en|algebra|ring theory}} The sum of the minimal [[normal]] [[submodule]]s of a given ''R''-[[module]] of a given [[ring]] ''R''.
# {{lb|en|group theory}} The [[subgroup]] generated by the minimal [[normal subgroup]]s of a given [[group]].

